# Zig style

Follow `STYLE.md` (repo root) for all new Zig and for lines you already touch. Do not restyle unrelated existing code.

Must:

- Run `zig fmt`. 4 spaces. Hard 100 columns. Soft 70 lines per function.
- Names: `TitleCase` types, `camelCase` functions, `snake_case` vars/namespaces. Type files `TitleCase.zig`.
- Prefer explicit widths. Use `usize` only for std lengths/indexes.
- Assert args, returns, pre/postconditions, invariants. Average two asserts per function. Split compound asserts.
- Handle every error. Recursion only with a hard depth or size limit.
- Pass library options at the call site; do not rely on defaults.

If STYLE.md and existing code disagree, keep the existing name/shape unless this change already has to rename that symbol.
